 "intro": "From Carthage to the Ottoman regencies, North Africa connects the continent to the Mediterranean world, and the Sahara connects it to the Sahel. Most of the written sources are outsiders' or enemies', so the skill of this module is reading them against their purpose and against the archaeology. Lecturer lens: Ibn Khaldun's life was spent among Maghribi dynasties. In 1384 the Egyptian sultan made him professor at the Qamhiyyah madrasa and chief Maliki judge in Cairo, where he found his reform efforts resisted. His group-feeling idea gives a lens for the Almoravids and Almohads.",
