 "intro": "Resistance did not end with conquest. Three cases show different forms: Maji Maji in German East Africa (1905 to 1907), the Herero and Nama war and genocide in German South West Africa (1904 to 1908), and the Mau Mau uprising in Kenya (1952 to 1960). Each is contested in numbers, causes and memory, and each sits in a wider pattern of risings, religious movements and tax flight across the continent. Lecturer lens: The same Boahen habit applies to resistance. Here we use it on Mau Mau, Maji Maji and the Herero and Nama war to decide which record answers which question.",
